  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Deep Ocean Iron Levels, 1997-present",
  "description": "Ambient dissolved and particulate iron levels in the deep ocean; part of a project to determine if iron is limiting to phytoplankton growth in the high-nutrient low chlorophyll waters of the subarctic Pacific Ocean. Surface-1000m\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: Measurement of ambient levels of iron in the deep ocean in high-nutrient, low chlorophyll waters to determine if iron is limiting to phytoplankton growth.\n\nSupplemental information: Risk Justification: Data not secured in regional data centre. Risk of Loss: Medium Impact Justification: Data are related to a subject, location or species of concern within the scientific, government or public community within the last 5 years. Impact of Loss: Medium Recommended Action: Obtain access to data and bring to archives. Additional Info: After the data are published, they may become available, if the Japanese collaborators agree to their release.",
